# The change log merges as ordinary text, on purpose. A `merge=union` driver
# never reports a conflict: when two branches edit the same entry it keeps
# both sides' lines, so the log silently gained duplicated and mis-attributed
# entries (#2042). A conflict at the top of the file is the expected cost of
# every branch prepending; how to resolve it is in the file's header comment.
# Do not re-add union, even where a tool recommends it.
.prawduct/change-log.md merge=text
